          "Spread the sample across the period, including busy weeks and thin coverage. Items drawn only from quiet weeks overstate the strength of the control. For each observation, record the time, reviewer, and source consulted. For a small population, state the count and uncertainty rather than a deceptive rate. A monthly sample reveals whether the rule survives a heavy week with partial coverage.",
          "Settle the evidence rule before seeing results: what source qualifies, what date attaches, how a blank is treated. Keep that rule in a short codebook beside the extract. CustomerSuccessManagers does not leave the rule in one person's memory. Written rules let a successor repeat the review without a handover call. Escalate the pattern rather than the individual case when the same gap recurs."
